  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only two challenging settings were confirmed, both at the top of the speed range with the crossing car 2 s late: scene 02eadd92 at 1.4x and +2 s (S4), and scene 054b5901 at 1.4x and +2 s (S9). The two fail in different ways. In 02eadd92, the ego ignores its RIGHT command, drifts into the left lanes and hits the retimed bus 127 head-on, so the crossing actor's timing does matter there. In 054b5901 the ego runs onto the median island, and the crossing car is never involved. Every 1.4x run on 054b5901 failed, whatever the timing, so speed rather than timing seems to drive that scene. The objective said to ignore failures unrelated to the crossing car, so S9 is a weak case. Every failure is flagged as a possible artifact because the ego ended more than 3.5 m off the recording. Triage blames the policy's leftward drift, not rendering. Still, above 1.0x the ego starts off the recording, so the simulator's share can't be fully ruled out.",
